{"world_model":"Simplest model: time ≈ fixed (~0.15–0.25 s) + steps × per-step cost, where per-step cost scales roughly with pixels, plus a memory-bound large-map component (BN/GELU/pool at 31×31). Accuracy ≈ a slowly rising function of total steps/epochs (~0.2 pp per 0.5 epoch, ~1.5–2.7 s/pp), with 3-seed noise ~0.1 pp (SE) and held-out 10-seed noise ~0.05–0.08 pp. Tip E027 (8.75 ep) has a held-out mean ~0.7526, below the 0.753 bar, so it sits at the margin; seeds 0–2 value 0.7547 is partly a lucky draw.

Misses explained: (1) Cutting compute that is memory-bound or in early layers (E028 freeze −0.5 s, E031 sample drop −0.6 s) saves more time than the MAC share, and the accuracy loss is only ~0.1–0.3 pp, which looks like the epoch-dial rate. (2) Averaging and regularization tweaks around Lookahead/EMA/LS (E025, E030, E032) hurt 0.3–0.7 pp: the airbench96 averaging and LS settings sit at a sharp, tuned optimum, so perturbations in either direction lose. Expect further averaging/LS tweaks to be negative or null. (3) Time is not strictly pixel-proportional; resolution changes at the early phase saved more than modelled (E026).

Supported mechanisms: early low-res is cheap (E026); the 32 px tail carries accuracy (E018, E011); the epoch dial is roughly linear; wd ×0.5 helped about 0.2 pp (E016); freeze/backward truncation saves ~8% time at a ~0.1–0.2 pp cost. Run-to-run: time noise ~±0.02 s; accuracy 3-seed noise ±0.15 pp; the seeds 0–2 draw changes whenever RNG use changes (the step count). Unsure: whether the freeze plus extra epochs nets positive; the winner's curse on seeds 3–12 selection; PCIe transfer.","forecasts":[{"idea":"I052","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.5,"point":5.72,"hi":5.95},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.75,"point":0.7535,"hi":0.7575}],"verdict":"inconclusive","reason":"Freeze saves ~0.5 s, +0.5 epoch costs ~0.3 s; the accuracy gain is about +0.2 pp but the freeze costs a bit, so it ends near the bar."},{"idea":"I053","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.75,"point":5.82,"hi":5.9},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.7515,"point":0.7547,"hi":0.7575}],"verdict":"supports","reason":"Math-identical systems change saves ~0.05 s if the outputs are bit-identical; accuracy is unchanged."},{"idea":"I054","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.2,"point":5.5,"hi":5.85},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.749,"point":0.7525,"hi":0.756}],"verdict":"inconclusive","reason":"Probably the whitening bias already stops at 3 epochs (whiten_bias_steps=3*steps_per_epoch, 33% of steps); stopping at 20% saves little, so the gain is small."},{"idea":"I055","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5,"point":5.2,"hi":5.45},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.747,"point":0.7505,"hi":0.7545}],"verdict":"inconclusive","reason":"An earlier freeze saves more time but costs more accuracy; it would likely land below the keep gate."},{"idea":"I056","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.8,"point":5.88,"hi":5.95},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.75,"point":0.7525,"hi":0.755}],"verdict":"supports","reason":"Diagnostic only; fresh seeds will regress toward the held-out mean of about 0.7525."},{"idea":"I057","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.1,"point":5.3,"hi":5.5},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.747,"point":0.75,"hi":0.753}],"verdict":"inconclusive","reason":"BN folding saves some memory traffic but is complex, and it carries the freeze's accuracy cost."},{"idea":"I058","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.8,"point":5.88,"hi":5.95},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.7515,"point":0.7547,"hi":0.7575}],"verdict":"supports","reason":"Diagnostic only; the profile will most likely show a large non-GEMM share on the big maps."},{"idea":"I059","metrics":[{"metric":"time","lo":5.55,"point":5.7,"hi":5.85},{"metric":"accuracy","lo":0.738,"point":0.745,"hi":0.752}],"verdict":"supports","reason":"Replacing Muon with SGD likely loses 0.3–1 pp, since E006 gave +0.66 pp, and saves ~3% time."}],"hypotheses":[{"id":"H2.6.2","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H3.2.1","outcome":"supported"},{"id":"H2.6.3","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H2.6.4","outcome":"refuted"},{"id":"H2.6.5","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H6.3.1","outcome":"supported"},{"id":"H6.3","outcome":"supported"},{"id":"H1.2.2","outcome":"supported"},{"id":"H4.3.2","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H1.3.5","outcome":"refuted"},{"id":"H1.3.6","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H1.3.8","outcome":"refuted"},{"id":"H1.5.5","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H1.5.6","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H2.3.6","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H2.3.7","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H5.1.1","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H5.1.2","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H2.6.6","outcome":"unknown"},{"id":"H2.3.5","outcome":"supported"}],"cruxes":["Does the freeze (E028) cost accuracy beyond the held-out noise, or is it neutral? If it is neutral, stacking it with epochs yields time gains of ~0.3 s.","Is the tip's true population mean ≥0.753 on fresh seeds (13–22)? The held-out figure of 0.7526 says no, so any further time cut needs an accuracy booster first.","Is the whitening bias already frozen early in the code (3 epochs ≈ 33% of steps)? That decides whether H2.6.3 has any lever left."]}
